{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b155a00fa7ab0ba5","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Distributed Workloads\n2\t\n3\t**Jira component**: Distributed Workloads\n4\t**Maturity**: Stable (GA); topology-aware scheduling Tech Preview\n5\t**Owning team**: Distributed Workloads\n6\t**Upstream**: kubernetes-sigs/kueue, project-codeflare/codeflare-operator, ray-project/kuberay\n7\t**Midstream**: opendatahub-io/kueue, opendatahub-io/codeflare-operator, opendatahub-io/kuberay\n8\t**Konflux onboarded**: yes\n9\t\n10\t## Role in the platform\n11\t\n12\tQueueing and orchestration layer for batch AI workloads. Kueue is the platform's\n13\tqueueing system (ClusterQueue/LocalQueue quota model, all-or-nothing admission\n14\tvia waitForPodsReady); Volcano is not shipped or supported. KubeRay manages Ray\n15\tclusters; CodeFlare SDK is the user-facing entry point for Ray-based jobs.\n16\t\n17\t## Dependencies\n18\t\n19\t- cert-manager for Kueue webhooks\n20\t- NVIDIA GPU Operator for GPU resource discovery and time-slicing configuration\n21\t\n22\t## Interfaces\n23\t\n24\t- ClusterQueue, LocalQueue, Workload CRDs (kueue.x-k8s.io)\n25\t- RayCluster/RayJob CRDs (ray.io); PyTorchJob admission via Kueue integration\n26\t- Kueue metrics (pending/admitted workloads per queue) exposed to Prometheus\n27\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ad147caad4d0d177","agent_id":"a717c353ff412c7c7","session_id":"d5dcf521-f769-4ae5-8dc7-46406c9edf08","uuid":"3fb147d4-e1ba-4fb5-be4e-2e0da472a071","timestamp":"2026-10-25T18:59:34.995Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b155a00fa7ab0ba5","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9018 into epics"}
