{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-aa162b0c28461b0a","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tname: epic-decompose\n3\tdescription: Decompose batches of RHAISTRAT strategies into implementation epic DAGs. Use when given RHAISTRAT strategy IDs or a JQL query selecting strategies to decompose into epics. Accepts explicit IDs or a JQL query. Non-interactive.\n4\tuser-invocable: true\n5\tallowed-tools: Glob, Bash, Agent\n6\t---\n7\t\n8\tYou are a non-interactive epic decomposition pipeline. Do not ask questions or wait for confirmation. Make all decisions autonomously.\n9\t\n10\t## Turn Discipline (critical)\n11\t\n12\tYou run headless. **A response that contains only text and no tool call ends the session and aborts the pipeline mid-run.** Until the dispatch loop returns `done`, every one of your turns MUST end with a tool call — never with prose.\n13\t\n14\tIn particular, after you launch a wave's Agent(s), do **not** write narration such as \"the agent is running, waiting for it to complete.\" That text-only turn terminates the pipeline before the wave is collected. Your very next action, in the **same turn** as (or immediately after) the launch, MUST be the `wait-for-wave` Bash call. Do not describe what you are about to do — do it. Save any commentary for after the pipeline reaches `DONE`.\n15\t\n16\t## Setup\n17\t\n18\tParse `$ARGUMENTS` for:\n19\t- `--jql \"<query>\"`, `--limit N`, `--batch-size N` (default 25), `--data-dir \"<path>\"`\n20\t- `--headless`, `--announce-complete`, `--reprocess`, `--skip-if-has-epics`\n21\t- Remaining arguments: explicit RHAISTRAT IDs\n22\t\n23\t### 1. Init\n24\t\n25\t```bash\n26\tpython3 scripts/pipeline_state.py init [--batch-size N] [--headless] [--announce-complete]\n27\t```\n28\t\n29\t### 2. IDs\n30\t\n31\t**JQL mode** (`--jql`):\n32\t\n33\t```bash\n34\tpython3 scripts/fetch_strategy.py fetch \"<query>\" --ids-file tmp/pipeline-all-ids.txt [--limit N] [--data-dir \"<path>\"] [--sk