{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bc16a627ead8fbd0","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9018-E001\n3\ttitle: Metering data consumption contract for GPU chargeback reporting\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9018\n5\tcomponent: Dashboard\n6\tteam: RHOAI Dashboard\n7\ttype: Investigation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tinvestigation_signals:\n10\t  question_specificity: 1\n11\t  source_accessibility: 0\n12\t  local_runnability: 0\n13\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: -1\n14\t  human_judgment_required: -1\n15\timplementation_type: null\n16\tdependencies: []\n17\tai_signals: null\n18\tai_implementability: Low\n19\tai_implementability_score: -1\n20\tjira_key: null\n21\tbranch: null\n22\tgated_by: null\n23\tgate_failure_impact: null\n24\t---\n25\t# Metering data consumption contract for GPU chargeback reporting\n26\t\n27\t## Description\n28\t\n29\tResolve the open question of how GPU chargeback reporting consumes the\n30\tper-project GPU-hour metering data being delivered by the GPU usage metering\n31\tstrategy (RHAISTRAT-9990). The metering data schema is owned by that in-flight\n32\tstrategy and is not final until it lands; this investigation pins down what\n33\treporting can build against, in what form, and with how much stability, so\n34\tthat the report implementation is not built against a moving target.\n35\t\n36\t## Scope\n37\t\n38\t- Engage with the owners of the GPU usage metering effort to identify the\n39\t  current metering data schema, its access path, and its finalization\n40\t  timeline.\n41\t- Produce a documented consumption contract for reporting: the fields,\n42\t  semantics, and access mechanism that the chargeback report implementation\n43\t  will build against, tied to a specific schema version or agreed snapshot.\n44\t- Assess schema stability and record a verdict with explicit criteria:\n45\t  stable enough to build against directly, in flux (build behind an isolating\n46\t  adapter with contract tests), or not yet consumable (defer the\n47\t  metering-dependent implementation work).\n48\t- Document the rework impact on report implementation and fallback options\n49\t  for each verdict.\n50\t- Deliverable: a consumption contract document with stability verdict and\n51\t  recommendation.\n52\t\n53\t## Acceptance Criteria\n54\t\n55\t- A consumption contract document exists that names the metering schema\n56\t  version or agreed snapshot, the fields and semantics of per-project\n57\t  GPU-hour data, and the access path reporting will use.\n58\t- The stability verdict is recorded (stable / in flux / not consumable) with\n59\t  the explicit criteria used to decide it, together with the corresponding\n60\t  recommendation for the report implementation.\n61\t- Rework impact and a fallback approach are documented for the in-flux and\n62\t  not-consumable cases.\n63\t- Risks arising from RHAISTRAT-9990 finalization timing and their effect on\n64\t  chargeback reporting delivery are recorded.\n65\t\n66\t## HLR Traceability\n67\t\n68\t- HLR-1 (P0): de-risks the data foundation for per-project GPU-hour\n69\t  consumption reports; the reports themselves are implemented downstream.\n70\t- Strategy Open Question 1 (metering schema finalization / external timing\n71\t  risk): this investigation is the resolution vehicle.\n72\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bd764de1121b3252","agent_id":"a416f59fcb1684ab3","session_id":"d5dcf521-f769-4ae5-8dc7-46406c9edf08","uuid":"bbf90be8-1690-4b6e-8f84-662c10033afe","timestamp":"2026-10-25T19:15:37.983Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-bc16a627ead8fbd0","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Re-review revised RHAISTRAT-9018"}
