{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ab23b770f3c83865","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9018-E002\n3\ttitle: 'GPU chargeback report service: computation, report API, and CSV export'\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9018\n5\tcomponent: Dashboard\n6\tteam: RHOAI Dashboard\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-9018-E001\n11\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-9018-E001\n12\tgate_failure_impact:\n13\t  action: rewrite\n14\t  fallback_approach: If the metering data schema is still in flux, rebuild the data\n15\t    access layer against the updated consumption contract behind an isolating adapter\n16\t    with contract tests; if the data is not yet consumable, defer this epic and its\n17\t    dependents until the metering strategy lands.\n18\tai_signals:\n19\t  change_specificity: 0\n20\t  pattern_precedent: 0\n21\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n22\t  existing_foundation: 1\n23\t  open_questions: -1\n24\t  external_dependency: -1\n25\t  human_process_gates: 0\n26\t  repo_access: 1\n27\t  architecture_claims: 1\n28\timplementation_type: null\n29\tinvestigation_signals: null\n30\tai_implementability: Medium\n31\tai_implementability_score: 1\n32\tjira_key: null\n33\tbranch: null\n34\t---\n35\t# GPU chargeback report service: computation, report API, and CSV export\n36\t\n37\t## Description\n38\t\n39\tDeliver the reporting backend for GPU chargeback: computation of per-project\n40\tGPU-hour consumption over selectable time ranges from the metering data,\n41\tserved through a stable API for the Dashboard administrator view and finance\n42\ttooling, with CSV export. Also surfaces each project's Kueue quota alongside\n43\tmetered consumption so the administrator view can present consumption against\n44\tquota.\n45\t\n46\t## Scope\n47\t\n48\t- Data access to per-project GPU-hour metering data per the metering data\n49\t  consumption contract agreed for this strategy (fields, semantics, access\n50\t  path, and schema stability verdict).\n51\t- Computation of per-project GPU-hour consumption totals over\n52\t  administrator-selectable time ranges.\n53\t- A stable API serving report data (per project, per time range) for the\n54\t  Dashboard administrator view and for finance tooling integration.\n55\t- CSV export of reports retrievable via the same report API.\n56\t- Inclusion of each project's Kueue quota alongside metered consumption in\n57\t  the report data, so consumption can be shown against quota.\n58\t\n59\t## Acceptance Criteria\n60\t\n61\t- Given a test dataset of metering data conforming to the agreed consumption\n62\t  contract, the computed per-project GPU-hour totals match expected values\n63\t  for a defined set of time ranges (pass/fail on the test dataset).\n64\t- Report data is retrievable via the report API for arbitrary projects and\n65\t  administrator-selected time ranges.\n66\t- Reports can be exported as CSV via the report API, and the CSV content\n67\t  carries the same figures as the corresponding API response.\n68\t- Each project's Kueue quota is included in the report data alongside its\n69\t  metered consumption.\n70\t- The data access layer conforms to the agreed metering data consumption\n71\t  contract; any deviation from the contract is documented and resolved before\n72\t  the change is merged.\n73\t\n74\t## HLR Traceability\n75\t\n76\t- HLR-1 (P0): per-project GPU-hour consumption reports over selectable time\n77\t  ranges — computation and serving.\n78\t- HLR-2 (P1, bundled): CSV export and stable API for finance tooling —\n79\t  bundled with HLR-1 because the export and the report API are presentation\n80\t  modes of the same report-serving surface this epic builds; splitting would\n81\t  build the same endpoint twice.\n82\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bd764de1121b3252","agent_id":"a416f59fcb1684ab3","session_id":"d5dcf521-f769-4ae5-8dc7-46406c9edf08","uuid":"1e9eb037-5e49-4fb0-9780-1486d9633b2b","timestamp":"202