{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b880b37b415f4517","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9018-E004\n3\ttitle: Kueue quota semantics validation for chargeback reporting\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9018\n5\tcomponent: Distributed Workloads\n6\tteam: Distributed Workloads\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-9018-E002\n11\tai_signals:\n12\t  change_specificity: 0\n13\t  pattern_precedent: 0\n14\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n15\t  existing_foundation: 1\n16\t  open_questions: 0\n17\t  external_dependency: 0\n18\t  human_process_gates: 0\n19\t  repo_access: 1\n20\t  architecture_claims: 1\n21\timplementation_type: null\n22\tinvestigation_signals: null\n23\tai_implementability: High\n24\tai_implementability_score: 3\n25\tjira_key: null\n26\tbranch: null\n27\tgated_by: null\n28\tgate_failure_impact: null\n29\t---\n30\t# Kueue quota semantics validation for chargeback reporting\n31\t\n32\t## Description\n33\t\n34\tAs the owning team of the Distributed Workloads queueing layer, validate that\n35\tthe Kueue quota figures used by GPU chargeback reporting are semantically\n36\tcorrect: the per-project quota carried in the chargeback report data\n37\talongside metered consumption must reflect\n38\tthe actual Kueue quota model of the platform's queueing configuration.\n39\t\n40\t## Scope\n41\t\n42\t- Define the correctness criteria mapping projects to their effective Kueue\n43\t  quota (LocalQueue/ClusterQueue quota model) as used by the chargeback\n44\t  reporting.\n45\t- Validate the quota figures carried in the chargeback report data produced\n46\t  by the report service (each project's Kueue quota reported alongside its\n47\t  metered consumption) against the actual queueing configuration, across\n48\t  representative project/quota setups. The validation anchors on the report\n49\t  data, so it runs in parallel with the administrator view work rather than\n50\t  waiting for the view to be built.\n51\t- Document any discrepancies with severity, and report them back to the\n52\t  chargeback reporting implementation for correction.\n53\t\n54\t## Acceptance Criteria\n55\t\n56\t- A validation report exists covering representative project/quota\n57\t  configurations, comparing the quota figures carried in the chargeback\n58\t  report data against the actual Kueue quota configuration.\n59\t- Every discrepancy found is documented with severity and reported to the\n60\t  chargeback reporting implementation.\n61\t- The Distributed Workloads team records a sign-off on the quota semantics\n62\t  used by chargeback reporting, or a list of blocking discrepancies that\n63\t  prevents sign-off.\n64\t\n65\t## HLR Traceability\n66\t\n67\t- HLR-3 (P1): correctness of the Kueue quota side of the current-month\n68\t  consumption-vs-quota administrator view.\n69\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bd764de1121b3252","agent_id":"a416f59fcb1684ab3","session_id":"d5dcf521-f769-4ae5-8dc7-46406c9edf08","uuid":"78cff6bd-8902-4127-9368-9cafbe4ed2ae","timestamp":"2026-10-25T19:15:44.664Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b880b37b415f4517","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Re-review revised RHAISTRAT-9018"}
